# =====================================================================
# .gitattributes — line endings, and what GitHub counts as our work.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# LINE ENDINGS
#
# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every
# platform. This is not tidiness. The team works across Windows and macOS,
# and the security suite compares index.html against site-original/index.html
# line by line. When one of those two files is checked out with CRLF and the
# other is not, a plain `diff` reports EVERY line as changed — roughly 6,000
# of them — and the real difference is invisible underneath the noise.
#
# If you are on Windows and a diff still shows the whole file, your working
# copy predates this rule. Either re-normalise:
#     git add --renormalize .
# or read the diff with:
#     diff --strip-trailing-cr site-original/index.html index.html
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# BINARY
#
# Named explicitly rather than left to auto-detection. A PNG that git decides
# to "normalise" is a corrupt PNG, and the emblem and social-preview images
# in assets/brand/ are the ones a judge sees first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.zip   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE LANGUAGE BAR ON GITHUB SHOWS
#
# Left alone, the bar at the top of the repository page is dominated by two
# things nobody on this team wrote: the vendored copies of Leaflet and
# supabase-js, and site-original/index.html, which is a frozen second copy of
# a page that is already counted once. Marking them vendored removes them
# from the statistics only. It does not hide them, does not exclude them from
# search, and does not collapse their diffs — an accidental edit to
# site-original/ must still be visible in a pull request, because that folder
# is the historical baseline the whole integration story rests on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
vendor/**        linguist-vendored
site-original/** linguist-vendored

# The security work is SQL — the tables, the row-level security policies, the
# column grants, the rate limits. Linguist classifies SQL as "data" and leaves
# it out of the bar by default, which understates 03's contribution to
# roughly zero. This puts it back.
*.sql linguist-detectable=true

# Markdown is deliberately NOT forced into the bar. There is a great deal of
# it here and it would swamp the code, which would misrepresent the project
# in the other direction.
